.TH ISA-PREFLIGHT 8 "November 2026" "isa-preflight 0.1" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
isa-preflight \- verify processor features or chain-load an init program
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B isa-preflight
is a static executable intended to run as the first userspace program in an
initramfs. On x86-64 variant builds, it checks the CPU flags of every processor
reported in
.I /proc/cpuinfo
and mounts
.I /proc
if necessary. If a required flag is missing, it reports the missing features
and halts the system. If all checks pass, it executes the configured successor
with its original arguments and environment.
.PP
The architecture variant and its required flags are compiled into the
executable. When built without a variant, the executable skips CPU checking and
only chain-loads the configured successor. The executable does not contain a
distribution-specific init path.
.SH BUILD-TIME CONFIGURATION
.TP
.I DEB_HOST_ARCH_VARIANT
Selects the architecture variant during a package build. An empty value builds
a generic static no-op chainloader on every architecture. Nonempty variant
builds currently support x86-64.
.TP
.I -Dvariant=VARIANT
Selects the variant for direct Meson builds.
.TP
.I VARIANTTABLE
Specifies dpkg's variant table during a package build, defaulting to
.IR /usr/share/dpkg/varianttable .
The selected row supplies the variant name and comma-separated Linux CPU flags.
For direct Meson builds, use
.IR -Dvarianttable=PATH .
.SH RUNTIME CONFIGURATION
The configuration directory is
.IR /etc/isa-preflight .
.TP
.I next-init
A single line containing the absolute path of the executable to run after a
successful check. The original argument vector and environment are preserved.
LF and CRLF line endings are accepted.
.SH EXIT BEHAVIOR
A successful check does not return: the successor replaces
.B isa-preflight
via
.BR execve (2).
Configuration errors and unsupported processors cause a diagnostic followed by
a system halt when running as PID 1. When running with another PID, or if
halting is unavailable, the program pauses indefinitely.
.SH NOTES
The x86-64 variant checker is freestanding and compiled for the base x86-64
instruction set so that its own instructions do not require the variant being
checked.
